Americans shouldn’t be paying the highest drug prices in the world. But cutting prices alone won’t fix a healthcare system driven by chronic disease. 

If Big Pharma’s answer to lower prices is selling more prescriptions... are we solving the problem or making it worse?

@JennGalardi is a Senior Policy Analyst for Restoring American Wellness at The Heritage Foundation.

