Birth tourism was never the intent of the 14th Amendment. So why is it still being treated as a pathway to U.S. citizenship?

Congress is weighing whether immigration status should matter when determining birthright citizenship, and the outcome could reshape one of the nation's most contentious immigration debates.

@lora_ries is Director of the Border Security and Immigration Center at The Heritage Foundation.

